---
description: Prevent new backend architecture debt during ordinary feature work.
---

<!-- coherent:prevention -->
Before adding a service, abstraction, DTO, helper, dependency, boolean, fallback, compatibility path, or layer: search for the existing authoritative concept or representation.

After implementing: search for code the change made obsolete.

Never preserve architecture only because many files already use it. Never merge two concepts only because they have similar shapes.

Inspect the affected diff and contracts: did this feature make the workflow harder to change? Run `coherent check --changed` only when the project explicitly requires its advanced baseline gate. A baseline is not required for ordinary work.

Do not run a full legacy cleanup for a small feature. Existing debt is allowed; new debt is not ignored.
<!-- /coherent:prevention -->
